&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Saudi Arabian authorities have transferred the flydubai co-pilot accused of stabbing the flight captain during a mid-air assault to the United Arab Emirates (UAE). The handover comes as authorities investigate the circumstances and motive behind the attack on the commercial flight, which was travelling to Israel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;According to Fox News, the aircraft lost thousands of feet in altitude after the captain was stabbed. Passengers then intervened to restrain the suspect, while other pilots aboard the aircraft took control and stabilised the flight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;All 174 people on board survived the incident. UAE authorities are investigating the attack and are also examining whether it had any connection to terrorism, Fox News reported.&lt;/p&gt;
